{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[B]Way up on the mountain In the sweet southern air
[E]Is where I seem to lose loads I have to [B]bear
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[B]Silence of the snow fall and the peacefulness around
[E]I feel so blessed with all that I have [B]found
[E]I feel so blessed with all that I have [B]found
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[E]Holler in the moonlight
[E]Sip the mountain [B]shine
[E]The sound of the music playin'
[E]Everything so [B]fine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Lookin' up a trail for a sign as I travel there
A liquor still, an old deer trail, or the home of a big old bear
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
Wouldn't want to mess with him because it is his home
He's like me he's better left alone
He's like me he's better left alone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Fishin' in the river at the bottom of these hills
Helps me find my peace of mind In all these natural frills
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
These mountains were the first to show their face up to the sky
Lay me to rest here when I die
Lay me to rest here when I die
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
Chorus then “Lay me to rest here when I die” x3
{end_of_verse}
